#===============================================================================
# @TYPE:       s0-opt-freq
# @FUNCTIONAL: B3LYP
# @BASIS:      6-31G(d)
# @SOLVENT:    CPCM(Methanol)
# @DISPERSION: D3BJ
# @ORCA:       6.1.0 (libXC 7.0.0)
# @CHARGE:     1
# @MULT:       1
# @SYSTEM:     closed-shell organic chromophore (C22-C26)
# @VERIFIED:   2026-05-08 — LSH-33, LSH-34 S₀ Opt+Freq, zero imag freq
#===============================================================================
# TEMPLATE: S₀ Ground State Geometry Optimization + Frequency Calculation
# Dispersion   : D3BJ (Becke-Johnson damping)
# Solvent      : CPCM (Methanol) — implicit solvent model
# Aux Basis    : Auto (RIJCOSX uses def2/J automatically)
#===============================================================================
# ORCA VERSION : 6.1.0 (Release, libXC 7.0.0)
# DATE TESTED  : 2026-05-08
# STATUS       : VERIFIED — LSH-33, LSH-34 S₀ Opt+Freq passed with zero imag freq
#===============================================================================
# KEYWORDS EXPLAINED:
#   Opt         Geometry optimization (minimization of S₀ PES)
#   Freq        Numerical frequencies after optimization (check for imag modes)
#   B3LYP       Hybrid GGA functional (20% HF exchange) — natively supported
#   RIJCOSX     RI for Coulomb + COSX for exchange (speedup, minimal accuracy loss)
#   6-31G(d)    Pople double-zeta + polarization on heavy atoms
#   D3BJ        Grimme's D3 dispersion correction with Becke-Johnson damping
#   CPCM(...)   Conductor-like Polarizable Continuum Model (solvent=MeOH)
#   TightOpt    Tighter convergence criteria for optimization
#   TightScf    Tighter SCF convergence (1e-8 Eh vs default 1e-6)
#===============================================================================
# POST-RUN CHECKS:
#   1. grep "HURRAY" <out>              → optimization converged
#   2. grep "imaginary perturbations"   → should be 0
#   3. grep "FINAL SINGLE POINT ENERGY" → last line = S₀ energy
#   4. Check <basename>.xyz exists      → optimized geometry
#   5. Check <basename>.hess exists     → Hessian for later ESD-VG
#===============================================================================

! Opt Freq B3LYP RIJCOSX 6-31G(d) D3BJ CPCM(Methanol)
! TightOpt
! TightScf

%maxcore 3072

%pal
   nprocs 16
end

* xyz 1 1
  <INSERT S₀ INITIAL GEOMETRY HERE — charge=1, mult=1 for closed-shell organics>
*